{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"82d457a77f8ac3a07604fb3f3984308421637ce28685eb1a2df0eeef747dde6f","digest":{"component_or_area":"review-bot shutdown lifespan","key_entities":["src/rebar/review_bot/app.py","reconcile.reconcile_once","reconcile.request_stop","reconcile.review_in_flight","voter.in_flight_reviews","queue.join","shutdown_drain_seconds","shutdown_cancel_seconds","_stop_requested","reconcile_loop"],"problem_keywords":["shutdown drain","reconciler review","in-flight work","graceful shutdown","task cancellation","drain timeout"],"propositions":["The lifespan drain awaits queue.join() only, missing the reconciler's inline review_and_vote, so reconciler tasks are cancelled within ~10s if the queue is empty regardless of review duration.","Container stop paths (manual docker compose, host reboot, systemd stop, autodeploy rollback) can kill in-flight reconciler reviews with no drain, and the reconciler retries silently without emitting VOTER_ERROR.","The shutdown drain must cover in-flight reconciler work bounded by the existing shutdown_drain_seconds() budget, and must not allow new reviews to start once shutdown begins.","After shutdown completes, the stop flag must be cleared so subsequent reconcile_once calls in the same process do not silently drop candidates."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787647431372110822,"uuid":"6f59a495-0304-4a1a-bb17-90fe9b105405"}